steinlens.button=Lens...
steinlens.dynamicFov=Dynamic FOV
steinlens.dynamicFov.hint=Changes the field of view when sprinting, with the Speed effect and when drawing a bow
steinlens.zoom=Zoom
steinlens.zoom.hint=Hold %s to zoom (change the key in Controls > Lens)
steinlens.zoomSmooth=Smooth camera on zoom
steinlens.zoomSmooth.hint=Turns on the smooth camera while zooming
steinlens.customItems=Enchantment textures
steinlens.customItems.hint=Item and armor textures by enchantment, from the resource pack: %s rule(s)
steinlens.glint=Glint
steinlens.glint.near=Near only
steinlens.glint.hint=Enchantment glint. Near only: no glint on armor and items farther than %s blocks; always in your hand and inventory
steinlens.armor=Armor
steinlens.armor.shown=Shown
steinlens.armor.hidden=Hidden
steinlens.armor.hint=Hides armor worn by players and mobs, including yours
steinlens.nametags=Nametags
steinlens.nametags.default=Default
steinlens.nametags.blocks=%s blocks
steinlens.nametags.hint=How far names above players and mobs are shown (game default: 64 blocks)
steinlens.default=Default
steinlens.compactAngles=Compact angles
steinlens.compactAngles.hint=Sine and cosine for animations from a 16x smaller table that fits in the CPU cache; slightly less precise animations
steinlens.fog=Fog
steinlens.fog.light=Light
steinlens.fog.hint=Terrain distance fog. Light: only at the edge of the render distance. Water, lava and blindness don't change
steinlens.cloudHeight=Cloud height
steinlens.cloudHeight.blocks=+%s blocks
steinlens.cloudHeight.hint=Raises the cloud layer above the game's height (128)
steinlens.keep=Extended distance
steinlens.keep.memory=Memory
steinlens.keep.disk=Disk
steinlens.keep.hint=Chunks the server discards stay on screen up to your render distance. Disk: saved per server and world, they come back on the next visit (distant ones are a still image). Changing worlds clears the memory
steinlens.keepLimit=Storage limit
steinlens.keepLimit.hint=How much terrain to keep, in memory and on disk; past the limit, the farthest (memory) and oldest (disk) are removed first
steinlens.connectedTextures=Connected blocks
steinlens.connectedTextures.hint=Connected textures from the resource pack (glass, bookshelves...): %s rule(s)
steinlens.chunkUploads=Chunks per frame
steinlens.chunkUploads.hint=How many finished chunks go to the GPU per frame. With a limit, a burst of arriving chunks spreads over more frames: terrain appears more slowly, without stutters
steinlens.waitNeighbors=Wait for neighbors
steinlens.waitNeighbors.hint=Only builds a chunk once the 8 around it have arrived: one build per chunk instead of 3 to 5. The outer ring of loaded chunks is not shown
steinlens.directRender=Direct rendering
steinlens.directRender.hint=Draws straight to the window, without copying the game's intermediate image every frame. Turns off spectator and F4 shaders
steinlens.graphicsApi=API
steinlens.graphicsApi.hint=Graphics API in use. Choose it in the Stein Client settings, before opening the game. Vulkan is the default; the game uses OpenGL only where Vulkan cannot run
steinlens.graphicsApi.unavailable=Vulkan did not start on this computer (%s), so the game is using OpenGL
steinlens.graphicsApi.reason.no_driver=no Vulkan driver
steinlens.graphicsApi.reason.no_window=the window system refused Vulkan
steinlens.graphicsApi.reason.no_device=no graphics card with Vulkan 1.2
steinlens.graphicsApi.reason.old_driver=graphics driver too old for Vulkan
steinlens.graphicsApi.crashed=The last time the game started with Vulkan it closed before showing the game, so it went back to OpenGL. Choose Vulkan again in the Stein Client to try once more
steinlens.graphics=Graphics
steinlens.graphics.fast=Fast
steinlens.graphics.fancy=Fancy

# Video settings topics
steinlens.topic.general=General
steinlens.topic.camera=Camera and players
steinlens.topic.light=Light and shadows
steinlens.bloom=Bloom
steinlens.bloom.low=Low
steinlens.bloom.high=High
steinlens.bloom.hint=A soft glow around the brightest parts of the world (sky near the sun, torches, lava). The HUD and menus don't change
steinlens.smoothEdges=Smooth edges
steinlens.smoothEdges.hint=Smooths the jagged outlines of blocks, players and items against what is behind them. Textures stay pixel-sharp
steinlens.hdr=HDR
steinlens.hdr.hint=On an HDR screen, lights (sun, torches, lava) shine brighter than the white of the menus. Needs Vulkan and HDR turned on in Windows display settings
steinlens.hdrWhite=HDR brightness
steinlens.hdrWhite.hint=How bright the white of the menus and the daylit world is with HDR. Set it close to Windows' "SDR content brightness" so the menus look the same with and without HDR
steinlens.hdrPeak=Screen peak
steinlens.hdrPeak.hint=The brightest your screen can show (see its specs: HDR400, HDR600, HDR1000...). Lights bend softly towards it instead of turning into flat white
steinlens.nits=%s nits
steinlens.topic.sky=Sky and weather
steinlens.topic.textures=Textures
steinlens.topic.players=Players and items
steinlens.topic.performance=Performance
steinlens.rain=Rain
steinlens.rain.hint=Off: the game no longer draws rain or snow for you (no drops, splashes or rain sound, and a clear sky). The weather stays the same for the server and for the rest of the game
steinlens.graphics.hint=The game's Fast and Fancy modes. Each one also sets the game's own options: Fast turns off clouds, particles, smooth lighting and shadows and caps render distance at 8 chunks
steinlens.topic.animations=1.7 animations
steinlens.oldAnimations=1.7 animations
steinlens.oldAnimations.hint=The 1.7 animations, like the Old Animations mod, on your screen only: nothing changes in what is sent to the server. Each part below can be toggled separately
steinlens.oldBlockHit=Block hitting
steinlens.oldBlockHit.hint=The swing keeps showing while blocking with a sword, eating, drinking or drawing a bow; blocking with attack held on a block, the hand swings like in 1.7 (no mining, nothing sent to the server)
steinlens.oldItems=Held items
steinlens.oldItems.hint=Items in your hand in first person at the 1.7 position, a bit smaller and lower. Blocks don't change
steinlens.oldSwordBlock=Sword blocking
steinlens.oldSwordBlock.hint=The blocking sword in first person at the 1.7 position
steinlens.oldBow=Bow
steinlens.oldBow.hint=The bow in first person at the 1.7 position, idle and drawn
steinlens.oldRod=Fishing rod
steinlens.oldRod.hint=The fishing rod (and the carrot on a stick) in first person at the 1.7 position
steinlens.oldBlockPose=3rd person blocking
steinlens.oldBlockPose.hint=Blocking players with the 1.7 arm and sword: the arm without the inward turn and the sword across the front of the body
steinlens.oldArmorHurt=Armor hurt color
steinlens.oldArmorHurt.hint=Armor turns red together with the body when a player or mob takes damage, like in 1.7
steinlens.quality=Quality
steinlens.quality.fast=Fast
steinlens.quality.fancy=Fancy
steinlens.quality.medium=Medium
steinlens.quality.high=High
steinlens.quality.ultra=Ultra
steinlens.quality.custom=Custom
steinlens.quality.hint=Sets the other options at once, from the lightest (Fast) to the richest (Ultra): detail, light, clouds, particles, bloom, edges and texture filters. The render distance stays yours. Change one of them by hand and it becomes Custom
steinlens.topic.display=Display and HDR
steinlens.topic.world=World
steinlens.topic.image=Image
steinlens.hdrBlack=HDR shadows
steinlens.hdrBlack.hint=Lifts or deepens the darkest parts of the picture. Raise it if dark places look like a black blot
steinlens.anisotropy=Anisotropic filtering
steinlens.anisotropy.hint=Keeps floors and walls sharp when seen from afar and at an angle. Needs mipmaps (World tab); the higher, the sharper
steinlens.supersample=Shimmer-free pixels
steinlens.supersample.hint=Textures stop flickering in the distance and at an angle, and stay crisp up close. Needs mipmaps (World tab)
steinlens.sharpen=Sharpness
steinlens.sharpen.hint=Brings out the fine detail of the textures without halos around the edges
steinlens.sharpen.1=Low
steinlens.sharpen.2=Medium
steinlens.sharpen.3=High
steinlens.hdrLook=HDR style
steinlens.hdrLook.stein=Stein
steinlens.hdrLook.natural=Natural
steinlens.hdrLook.hint=Stein: soft colours, a little more vivid and moody, without hard contrast. Natural: the picture as the game draws it
steinlens.hdrQuality=HDR quality
steinlens.hdrQuality.quick=Quick
steinlens.hdrQuality.max=Maximum
steinlens.hdrQuality.hint=Quick: the picture as good, with much less cost on the graphics card (only the lights use the extra precision). Maximum: the whole picture in extra precision, for very lifted shadows
steinlens.dynamicLights=Dynamic lights
steinlens.dynamicLights.hint=A torch or glowstone in a hand, a light block dropped on the ground and burning creatures light what is around them, as if the block were there. Only on your screen
steinlens.atmosphere=Atmosphere
steinlens.atmosphere.1=Soft
steinlens.atmosphere.2=Strong
steinlens.atmosphere.hint=A mist that gathers low in the valleys and over the water, thicker at night and at dawn, and rays of sun (or moon) through the gaps of trees, mountains and clouds
steinlens.shadows=Sun shadows
steinlens.shadows.hint=The sun (and the moon) shine with a strong, warm light and everything casts a shadow: trees, buildings, hills, creatures and you yourself. In the shade, only the sky's cool light. Medium and up: creatures and players cast too; higher reaches farther and is sharper
steinlens.shadows.1=Low
steinlens.shadows.2=Medium
steinlens.shadows.3=High
steinlens.moonlight=Moonlight
steinlens.moonlight.hint=At night what is open to the sky gets a strong blue light from the moon, brighter at full moon. The world's real light (where mobs spawn) does not change
steinlens.darkness=Darkness
steinlens.darkness.hint=Where no torch, lamp, lava or sky light reaches, it is truly dark: a cave without a torch is black, and every light stands out. The world's real light (where mobs spawn) does not change
steinlens.glowingBlocks=Glowing blocks
steinlens.glowingBlocks.1=On
steinlens.glowingBlocks.2=Intense
steinlens.glowingBlocks.hint=The torch's flame, glowstone, lamps, the sea lantern, jack o'lanterns, lava, fire, the portal and the beacon truly shine, with a halo, brighter than anything lit (in HDR, above white); lava pulses and fire flickers. Intense: stronger, and the light is stronger right by the source, without reaching farther
